<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moriscos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Morisco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moriscos were Muslims of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> who had been forcibly converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and were eventually expelled in the early seventeenth century. Many settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>'s profile, Morisco refugees formed part of the Moroccan expeditionary force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judar-pasha">Judar Pasha</a> that invaded Songhai in 1591.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moriscos.jpg" alt="Moriscos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joanbanjo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%27expulsi%C3%B3_dels_moriscos_(1894),_Gabriel_Puig_Roda,_Museu_de_Belles_Arts_de_Castell%C3%B3_(detall).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
